# Keep every file's bytes EXACTLY as committed, on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text files to
# CRLF on checkout. That is normally harmless, but this repo pins the bytes of
# its vendored assets: starnix/build.mjs sha256-checks vendor/montserrat.css and
# vendor/three-r128.min.js and refuses to build on a mismatch. A CRLF checkout
# changes those bytes, so the build dies with
#
#     BUILD FAIL: vendor/montserrat.css drifted
#
# which reads like a supply-chain tamper alarm when the only thing that changed
# is line endings. `-text` disables the conversion so the pins keep matching.
#
# NOTE for anyone who already cloned on Windows before this file existed: adding
# it does NOT repair an existing working tree. Re-clone, or run
#     git rm --cached -r . && git reset --hard
* -text

# Belt and braces: never treat the pinned vendor assets as text under any rule.
starnix/vendor/** binary
wwtbane/vendor/** binary
